## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these terms, and the **software** is the software the licensor makes available under these terms.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these terms.

An **organization** includes a legal entity, sole proprietorship, partnership or other group working together, whether or not incorporated.

An **organization group** or **group** is the beneficiary organization together with every organization controlling it, controlled by it or under common control, worldwide. Consolidate 100% of controlled entities' figures, eliminate intra-group sales and funding transfers, and count each person once. Include acquired entities' measurement-period history on a pro-forma combined basis. Reorganizations, split invoices, subsidiaries and new installations do not reset history or thresholds. Unrelated clients or suppliers are not affiliates merely because they trade. Shared passive investment without control is not common control. Shared sovereignty alone does not combine a whole country: an independently administered public institution and its controlled operating subsidiaries form the public-body unit, subject to the commercial-operation separation above.

**Group people (H)** counts current full-time and part-time employees (including leave), working founders/owners, working officers/directors and unpaid people regularly performing business work. Assigned contractors or agency personnel count only while currently engaged and after working on more than 30 calendar days in the preceding 12 months; casual unpaid helpers use the same rule. Any work on a day counts as one day; counting begins on worked day 31 without reclassifying earlier use. A genuinely ended engagement stops counting; re-engagement retains prior days within the rolling period. Count identifiable assigned workers in any business function, not an entire outside supplier's staff merely because its services are bought. Customers, enrolled students, passive investors, bots, AI agents, accounts and machines do not count merely as such. A person **works for** an organization when they meet these workforce rules; that phrase does not limit permission for authorized short-term contractors to act for a client.

**Measurement date** is the relevant calendar month end; the **measurement period** is the 12 completed calendar months ending then. New businesses use actual figures since formation, without annualizing, until 12 months exist; acquisition/reorganization does not erase history. H is current at the measurement date; its contractor test uses the preceding 12 months.

**Revenue and funding (R)** is consolidated gross revenue from all business lines PLUS investment/grant funding raised during the measurement period, including equity investment, capital contributions, convertible notes, SAFEs and other instruments convertible into equity, and commercial grants (grants, subsidies or prizes received for business activity, as distinct from core-purpose grants under Education and Public Benefit). Ordinary bank loans are excluded. Other loans from owners, investors or their affiliates count as funding unless made on ordinary arm's-length commercial terms, and a loan later converted into equity or forgiven counts when converted or forgiven if it was not already counted. Funding counts in the month it is received, not again on conversion of a note or intra-group transfer; never count the same receipt twice as both revenue and funding. Funding valuation and cash balances are not receipts. For revenue, apply consistently recognized local accounting principles or IFRS/GAAP: deduct sales taxes collected for the state and actual refunds/returns, not wages, infrastructure, model costs, commissions or payment fees. Customer advances enter revenue when recognized, not twice on receipt and earning. Consistent principal-versus-agent accounting determines recognized marketplace revenue; neither profit nor gross merchandise value is automatically R. Convert non-USD revenue and funding using monthly average rates from the relevant central bank or another consistently applied public source; retain the source and calculation. Purpose-exempt funding is treated as specified in Education and Public Benefit, not as a reason to revoke that exception.

**Commercial operation** is an institution's economically connected business activity using the software, including paid proprietary development/consulting, product subscriptions, IP licensing and commercial data/services. Its **external commercial revenue (C)** is all recognized revenue of that activity, not merely incremental revenue attributed to the software, using R's revenue accounting and measurement period but excluding investment/funding and exempt core-purpose receipts. Combine connected operations under common institutional control; where honest separation is unavailable assess the combined relevant commercial activity, not an artificially small department. The separate R measure includes that operation's counted funding once the C trigger applies.

**Your organization** is the organization you are, if you are one, and any legal entity, sole proprietorship, partnership, or other kind of organization that you work for, plus all organizations that have control over, are under the control of, or are under common control with any of them.  This definition applies only to [Patent Defense](#patent-defense).

**Control** means more than 50% of voting power or actual power to direct management and policies, by contract or otherwise, directly or indirectly. Voting power and rights held by persons acting together under an agreement or arrangement, including through nominees, are combined. A passive minority holding alone is not control.

**Your licenses** are all the licenses granted to you for the software under these terms.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your licenses.
